WEBVTT

00:03:56.762 --> 00:04:00.307
I bet you pictured a far more classy and refined crowd.

00:04:00.307 --> 00:04:01.623
Blazers and skirts,

00:04:01.623 --> 00:04:03.026
wine and caviar.

00:04:03.594 --> 00:04:04.790
Why is this?

00:04:05.068 --> 00:04:09.261
How is it that phrases that are considered just about synonymous by the dictionary

00:04:09.261 --> 00:04:12.753
can evoke such different pictures and feelings?

00:04:12.753 --> 00:04:15.787
"Hearty" and "welcome" are both Saxon words.

00:04:15.787 --> 00:04:18.912
"Cordial" and "reception" come from French.

00:04:18.912 --> 00:04:22.447
The connotation of nobility and authority has persisted

00:04:22.447 --> 00:04:24.634
around words of French origin.

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:26.870
And the connotation of peasantry,

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:27.919
real people,

00:04:27.919 --> 00:04:28.966
salt of the Earth,

00:04:28.966 --> 00:04:32.091
has persisted around Saxon words.